# Copy to .env.local and fill in. Never commit real values.
# Local development against the local backend (Phase 05, see CLAUDE.md "Local development"):
# NEXT_PUBLIC_BACKEND_API_URL=http://localhost:3000/api plus FAKE Supabase values, e.g.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=https://supabase-placeholder.invalid and NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=local-placeholder-anon-key
# (.invalid never resolves). Public pages work; login does not work locally until the auth phase.

# NestJS backend base URL including /api. Used in development (browser and server; required there)
# and by server-side code in production. In production the browser does NOT use it: it calls the
# same-origin path /backend-api, which next.config.ts rewrites to BACKEND_ORIGIN.
NEXT_PUBLIC_BACKEND_API_URL=http://localhost:3000/api
# Optional (also on Vercel). Origin that /backend-api/* is proxied to, as <BACKEND_ORIGIN>/api/*.
# Default: https://api.nusantaralegacy.org (the production API). Must be https (http only for
# localhost), no path, no trailing slash; an invalid value fails `pnpm build`. Read at build time.
# BACKEND_ORIGIN=https://api.nusantaralegacy.org
# Optional, build time (Phase 29). Login implementation: "supabase" (default when unset or anything else)
# or "local" (the self-hosted backend login; no Supabase code in the build). Local mode outside Vercel needs
# BACKEND_ORIGIN (e.g. http://localhost:3000), see CLAUDE.md "Self-hosted login in the frontend (Phase 29)".
# NEXT_PUBLIC_AUTH_MODE=supabase
# Supabase project URL (needed for auth and for pnpm build prerendering).
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=
# Supabase anon (public) key for that project.
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=
# Optional, build time (Phase 25). "true" shows PROT documents (dokumenKurikulum) on public pages again.
# Default (unset or anything else): documents are shown only to reviewer roles. Files listed in
# lib/prot/hidden-media.ts are never shown, whatever this says.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SHOW_PROT_DOCUMENTS=false
